# The Node.js runtime bundled in Pako.app (desktop/mac/package.sh): the version, then the SHA-256 of each official tarball, as nodejs.org's
# SHASUMS256.txt for that version lists them. The build checks every download against these lines AND against SHASUMS256.txt, so a new
# version shows up here as a reviewed diff. To move to a newer Node.js 22 LTS: read https://nodejs.org/dist/index.json (newest v22.x with
# "lts"), copy its two darwin lines from https://nodejs.org/dist/<version>/SHASUMS256.txt, and if you have gpg, check that file's
# signature first (SHASUMS256.txt.sig, the release keys listed in https://github.com/nodejs/node#release-keys).
